      "paragraph_text": "Males with Y chromosome infertility have azoospermia or severe, moderate, or mild oligozoospermia depending on the location and size of the Y chromosome deletion (see Genotype-Phenotype Correlations ). Most males with AZFa or AZFb/c deletions have a very poor prognosis for finding any sperm with testicular sperm extraction (TESE). Males with AZFc deletions (b2/b4 or gr/gr) have an extremely favorable prognosis (87%) for finding sperm sufficient for successful intracytoplasmic sperm injection (ICSI).",
